          "answer": "SpaceBook-authored answer based on this unit (the textbook prints no answers):\nRoss let a female Anopheles mosquito bite a malarial patient and found Plasmodium multiplying in its stomach. He then used sparrows: a female Culex mosquito bit a sparrow with malaria; Plasmodium multiplied in the stomach wall and moved to the salivary glands. Infected mosquitoes bit healthy sparrows, which got malaria and had many Plasmodium in their blood.",
