          "Scientific Information",
          "DNA is also responsible for the transmission of characteristics to the next generation. That is why, it is called the hereditary material.",
          "The chromosomes are more visible in a dividing cell. In non-dividing cells, chromosomes are in the form of a network of fine threads known as chromatin network. Chromosomes are made of Deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA) and proteins. DNA controls all the activities of the cell. The chromosome number is always specific for a particular species.",
          "For example in human cell it is 46, in raddish 18 and in onion 16. The prokaryotic cells do not contain prominent nucleus. Rather, their chromosome is made of DNA only and is submerged in the cytoplasm.",
