          "It is the random movement of a substance from the region of higher concentration to the region of lower concentration. Cell membrane does not spend energy when molecules diffuse through it. That is why diffusion is a type of passive transport.",
          "Science, Technology and Society",
          "\"All diseases are disturbances at the cellular level\" (Rudolph Virchow, 1858). We always try to treat a disease and for this we try to find out the causes for the disease. We must understand the changes occurring at the cellular level to understand the cause of disease. The changes in the gene function may be the reasons for various disease. However, not all diseases are because of the gene functions such as infectious disease. In all diseases, cell biology is important from causes to treatments.",
          "Cell biology is important field of biological sciences. Studying cell biology may lead to a successful career. Cell biologist examines how the cell develops and how it works. Molecular biologist studies the molecules and processes inside the cells. Research specialist conducts and report research in the research laboratory. Laboratory technician assists the scientist in their research. A graduate of cell biology could be a Biology teacher who teaches cell biology at graduate and secondary school level.",
          "Only small molecules can diffuse through cell membrane e.g. water, carbon dioxide, oxygen and some other simple molecules. Diffusion is a slow process, yet it is efficient and rapid enough to fulfill the requirements of the cells. Substance such as glucose, O₂ and CO₂ can easily diffuse through the membrane. Glucose is present in higher concentration after the food is digested in small intestine. Therefore, glucose is transported to villi from the inner space of small intestine through diffusion to be stored in the form of glycogen in liver.",
