          "ans": "The Nucleus is the master control center of the eukaryotic cell:\n\n1. Nuclear Envelope:\n• A double-membrane barrier enclosing the nucleoplasm. The outer membrane is continuous with the rough endoplasmic reticulum.\n• Perforated by hundreds of Nuclear Pores composed of nucleoporin protein complexes that strictly regulate the bidirectional trafficking of RNA, ribosomal subunits, and regulatory proteins between nucleus and cytoplasm.\n\n2. Chromatin:\n• The diffuse network of genetic material composed of linear double-stranded DNA coiled around octamers of basic Histone proteins forming nucleosomes.\n• During cell division, chromatin condenses into distinct visible Chromosomes (e.g., 46 chromosomes in human diploid cells) containing genes that encode all cellular proteins.\n\n3. Nucleolus (Plural: Nucleoli):\n• A dense non-membranous dark-staining sub-compartment within the nucleus.\n• Functions as the ribosome factory: transcribes ribosomal RNA (rRNA) genes and assembles rRNA with imported ribosomal proteins into 40S and 60S ribosomal subunits.\n\n4. Nucleoplasm:\n• Viscous aqueous matrix containing dissolved nucleotides, enzymes (DNA and RNA polymerases), and mineral ions required for DNA replication and transcription."
