            "text": "In animals, the parent cells with diploid number of chromosomes undergo meiosis to produce haploid gametes, sperms in males and ova in females. The male and female gametes fuse together and make a zygote with diploid number. The zygote undergoes mitosis many times and develops into the new diploid organism.",
