            "text": "Respiration is defined as oxidation-reduction processes which occur inside the living cells during which organic food is broken down into carbon dioxide and water and energy is released. Glucose is the most common food used in this process. The purpose of respiration is to release energy for the living processes. Respiration is common to all living organisms because all of them need energy for life activities.",
