            "text": "In previous unit, we studied that all organisms need energy to perform their functions. We also know that they get this energy by the oxidation of food. Heterotrophs obtain food from others. On the other hand, autotrophs make their own food by photosynthesis. For making their food, autotrophs need to take essential materials from their environment.",
