        "content": [
          "In plants, water and dissolved salts are transported through the xylem tissue while organic food is transported through the phloem tissue.",
          "The root hair provide large surface area to the root for the maximum absorption of water and salts.",
          "Due to higher concentration of salts in root hair cells, water moves by passive transport i.e. osmosis.",
          "Loss of water in the form of vapours from the aerial parts of the plant, is called transpiration.",
          "Stoma opens when guard cells are turgid, while it closes when guard cells become flaccid.",
          "Transpiration of water from the leaves creates a pulling force in the leaves, called transpirational pull.",
          "According to the theory of Pressure Flow, in the plant body the dissolved food flows from a source to a sink.",
          "Blood is composed of two parts i.e. plasma (55% by volume) and blood cells or cell-like bodies (45% by volume).",
          "Blood plasma is about 90% water and 10% dissolved substances.",
          "Plasma proteins perform important functions e.g. albumins maintain osmotic pressure of blood, antibodies defend the body against pathogens, and fibrinogen is responsible for blood clotting.",
          "A cubic millimetre of blood contains about 5 million RBCs. Mature RBC is biconcave, rounded cell and contains no nucleus.",
          "WBCs are colourless, irregular in shape and are nucleated. Each cubic millimetre of blood contains about 7000 to 8000 WBCs.",
          "Platelets are fragments of cytoplasm pinched off from certain bone marrow cells. Each cubic millimetre of blood contains about 150,000 to 450,000 platelets.",
          "Leukaemia or blood cancer is a disease in which leucocytes or WBCs increase abnormally.",
          "Thalassaemia means formation of defective haemoglobin which cannot transport oxygen.",
          "A person having antigen A and anti-B antibodies has blood group A.",
          "A person having antigen B and anti-A antibody has blood group B.",
          "A person having both the antigens and no antibody has blood group AB.",
          "A person having neither antigen A nor antigen B and having both anti-A and anti-B antibodies has blood group O.",
          "A person having Rh antigen has blood group Rh+ve and a person lacking it has blood group Rh-ve.",
          "Heart is covered by a tough double membrane called pericardium.",
          "The heart of birds and mammals has two sides, each side divided into an upper chamber called atrium and lower chamber called ventricle.",
          "Right atrium communicates with right ventricle through a valve called tricuspid valve and left atrium opens into left ventricle through a bicuspid valve.",
          "A semilunar valve is present between each ventricles and large vessels.",
          "The right side of the heart collects deoxygenated blood from body and sends it to the lungs while the left side collects oxygenated blood from the lungs and sends it to the body.",
          "The flow of blood from heart to lungs and then from lungs to heart is called pulmonary circulation.",
          "The flow of blood from heart to the body tissues and then from body tissues to heart is called systemic circulation.",
          "Contraction of heart is termed as systole and relaxation as diastole. One complete cycle takes 0.8 seconds.",
          "A pulse is a series of expansion waves in an artery caused by the contractions of the left ventricle.",
          "All the arteries carry oxygenated blood except for pulmonary arteries which carry deoxygenated blood.",
          "The walls of an artery are made of three layers i.e. outer elastic layer, middle thick muscular layer and inner endothelium.",
          "The walls of capillaries are formed of single layer of cells i.e. endothelium.",
          "All the veins transport deoxygenated blood except for pulmonary veins which bring oxygenated blood.",
          "Veins also have valves which allow the flow of blood in one direction i.e. towards heart and prevent backward.",
          "The first arteries branching off from the aorta are coronary arteries which supply the oxygenated blood and food to heart itself.",
          "Atherosclerosis means narrowing of arteries due to the deposition of fatty material e.g. cholesterol inside the arteries.",
          "Arteriosclerosis means hardening of arteries due to the deposition of calcium in the walls of the arteries.",
          "Myocardial infarction occurs when the part of heart muscles cannot get the required oxygen and die.",
          "The symptom of chest pain due to lack of oxygen supply to the heart muscle is called angina pectoris"
        ],
